message: "If you use this software, algorithm, or dataset in your research, please cite it as below."
authors:
  - family-names: "TriNetra Research Initiative"
    given-names: "Core Team"
    affiliation: "TriNetra Open Science Project"
title: "TriNetra-Link: Deterministic Multimodal Chain-of-Custody Attribution Under Physical Degradation"
version: 2.6.0
date-released: 2026-10-26
url: "https://github.com/Sanjai-Quest/TriNetra_AI_Research"
keywords:
  - supply chain security
  - chain-of-custody
  - physical tamper detection
  - multimodal sensor fusion
  - selective abstention
  - audit integrity
license: "MIT"
abstract: >-
  TriNetra-Link is an algorithm and physical benchmark dataset for attributing
  custodial discrepancy stages in multi-transfer supply chains. Using a metadata-only
  quality gate, multimodal physical reconciliation (weight, identity, planar homography visual),
  and causal interval isolation (Algorithm 1), TriNetra-Link isolates the exact transition interval
  of physical tampering while appropriately abstaining when evidence is degraded or indistinguishable.
